.TH NLE 1 "" "NLE" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
nle \- run Windows x64 programs as native Linux programs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nle
[\fBrun\fR] [\fIoptions\fR] \fIapp.exe\fR [\fIargs\fR...]
.br
.B nle inspect
[\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-v\fR] \fIapp.exe\fR
.br
.B nle relink
\fIapp.exe\fR [\fB\-o\fR \fIDIR\fR] [\fIoptions\fR]
.br
.B nle gui
[\fIFOLDER\fR|\fIapp.exe\fR]
.br
.B nle coverage
[\fB\-\-markdown\fR|\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fILIB\fR]
.br
.B nle doctor
.br
.B nle binfmt
[status|install|remove]
.SH DESCRIPTION
NLE loads a Windows x86-64 executable into a Linux process and implements the Windows API it calls, without emulation.
Programs with windows are drawn by NLE's own window system and shown on an X11 display.
.PP
.B nle app.exe
runs a program. Its exit code is the program's.
.B nle inspect
reports which of the program's imports are implemented and gives a verdict (native, partial or unsupported).
.B nle relink
converts a program to a standalone Linux ELF that needs only libnle.so next to it.
.B nle gui
opens a window to browse for programs, inspect, run and relink them.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-backend " auto|native|wine"
Choose the native layer, or Wine for programs that need APIs NLE does not implement.
.TP
.BI \-\-prefix " DIR"
Root of the emulated C:\e drive.
.TP
.B \-\-strict
Refuse to start a program with unimplemented imports.
.TP
.B \-v
Explain which backend was chosen.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NLE_PREFIX
Directory tree used as the Windows drive (default: ~/.local/share/nle/prefix).
.TP
.B NLE_WINE
Path of the wine binary used as a fallback.
.TP
.B NLE_TRACE
Comma separated list of load, bind, api, all: debug logging.
.TP
.B NLE_GUI
x11 (default when DISPLAY is set) or headless.
.TP
.B NLE_GUI_SCRIPT
Script for the headless display (used by tests).
.TP
.B NLE_LIB
Path of libnle.so, used by relink.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/lib/nle/libnle.so
The runtime library that relinked programs load.
.SH SEE ALSO
https://github.com/SegMind25/NLE
